ally this  work i do like marcus buller at mit he's  been doing stuff with the sound of dna  and he's been doing um his most infamous  piece was he took the dna of the covid  virus and made a series of electronic  music pieces out of  the covet  uh  you know which  it it sounds like experimental  electronic music like no beats or  anything  um so the other thing is yeah i would  love to work with yale's environmental  department in fact hopefully we'll reach  out to them um over the next couple of  months  any other question  if not let's uh thank formula again  um i do want to just mention everybody  everything i'm talking about i'm a big  fan of what you call open source culture  so much of the work that i'm doing  is open source and on my website um  there's articles there's downloadable  material uh there's articles and books  uh my books are with mit  uh lately i've been really interested in  this idea of curating um  i just curated a big exhibition about  afrofuturism which is another art  movement that's pretty cool  uh and yeah i'm a big fan of the of the  dialect process so thank you guys so  much for coming out and i hope um to see  you guys over the next couple months
 

